OL,5,G1930 Radio 3 in Concert
OL,6,     FThe BBC Philharmonic Orchestra
OL,7,     Fwith chief conductor John
OL,8,     FStorgards at the Bridgewater Hall
OL,9,     Fin Manchester with music by
OL,10,     FCassandra Miller, Mendelssohn and
OL,11,     FMahler.
OL,12,G2145 The Essay: Symphony of the Wild
OL,13,     FMusic is thought to be unique to
OL,14,     Fhumans. But does it echo deeper
OL,15,     Finto nature? Ben Garrod discovers
OL,16,     Fsome remarkable rhythms coming
OL,17,     Ffrom some of earth's oldest
OL,18,     Fmusicians: plants.
